  "summary": "The schematic is a coherent ATtiny fan controller: the two MCU footprints (U1 ATtiny45-20P THT and U4 ATtiny13V-10S SMD) share identical, correct pin-to-net mappings (MISO/MOSI/SCK/RST on the ISP header J6 match PB1/PB0/PB2/PB5, and the I2C lines on J3 match the USI pins), the potentiometer (J4) feeds the ADC pin via NET0003, the high-side PMOS fan switch (Q2) with its level-shift driver Q3 and the VCC_STABLE jumper JP2 are wired sensibly, and the LM1117-5.0 (U3) takes VCC as input and produces the +5V rail (C2 on VCC, C3 on +5V). No deviation from the intended design is supported by the drawing."
}

